From a2f3fd1a471a13e05078c5eacfc9f77b328e8804 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanju Abraham <s.abraham@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:38:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(governance): HTTP CRUD endpoints
 /api/governance/users

Adds 5 endpoints mirroring /teams and /customers:

  GET    /api/governance/users
  POST   /api/governance/users
  GET    /api/governance/users/{user_id}
  PUT    /api/governance/users/{user_id}
  DELETE /api/governance/users/{user_id}

The list endpoint supports pagination (limit/offset), name+email
search (case-insensitive substring), and filter by team_id.

The Create endpoint accepts inline budget + rate_limit objects and
transactionally creates the rate_limit row, then the user row, then
the budget row (which has user_id FK). After commit the row is
re-fetched with relations preloaded and the in-memory cache is
populated via the GovernanceManager.ReloadUser callback.

Wiring:
- Adds CreateUserInMemory / UpdateUserInMemory / DeleteUserInMemory
  to the GovernanceStore interface so the server.go callbacks can
  invoke them without type-asserting on *LocalGovernanceStore.
- Adds ReloadUser / RemoveUser to the GovernanceManager interface
  (both declarations: handlers/governance.go and server/server.go).
- Implements ReloadUser / RemoveUser on BifrostHTTPServer.
- Adds matching stubs to the pricing_override_test mock.
